WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.700
Speaker 1: We have a voicemail number.

00:00:01.700 --> 00:00:02.969
That number is 2192.

00:00:02.969 --> 00:00:09.070
David, here is another viewer who has a parent
that they are struggling with when it comes

00:00:09.070 --> 00:00:10.780
to politics and media.

00:00:10.780 --> 00:00:13.760
But this is a little bit of a different problem
than one we've heard before.

00:00:13.760 --> 00:00:14.760
Take a listen to this.

00:00:14.760 --> 00:00:15.930
Speaker 5: David.

00:00:15.930 --> 00:00:19.610
I know you get these calls all the time.

00:00:19.610 --> 00:00:20.610
Yeah.

00:00:20.610 --> 00:00:23.550
How do I get my mother from Fox News?

00:00:23.550 --> 00:00:30.220
I mean, she's not so radical that she believes
in Q and A and and all this other crazy crap.

00:00:30.220 --> 00:00:33.850
But I can't get her to turn on Fox News.

00:00:33.850 --> 00:00:38.370
It's think it's just insane.

00:00:38.370 --> 00:00:44.449
And, I mean, as soon as I leave the house,
she turns this on.

00:00:44.449 --> 00:00:49.109
I mean, anyway, I try to point out to her,
you know, how wrong they are.

00:00:49.109 --> 00:00:51.390
And then, you know, things happen.

00:00:51.390 --> 00:00:54.499
I go, remember I told you they were wrong
about that.

00:00:54.499 --> 00:00:59.739
And, you know, and I told her, I said, See,
I'm right, about 90% of stuff and Fox News

00:00:59.739 --> 00:01:05.449
is wrong about 90% of stuff, but I can't get
her to turn it off.

00:01:05.449 --> 00:01:06.449
Yeah.

00:01:06.449 --> 00:01:07.890
Anyway, thanks, man.

00:01:07.890 --> 00:01:08.890
You do a great job.

00:01:08.890 --> 00:01:09.890
Speaker 1: Thank you.

00:01:09.890 --> 00:01:13.080
Well, so, listen, this this is tough, persistent
FOX News.

00:01:13.080 --> 00:01:17.680
Watching can be a hard habit to break or a
hard addiction to break.

00:01:17.680 --> 00:01:21.500
One of the things I would suggest, because
it sounds like your mom is really pretty deep

00:01:21.500 --> 00:01:26.369
into it instead of immediately trying to get
her off of Fox.

00:01:26.369 --> 00:01:30.840
What I would suggest is just that she diversify
the media diet.

00:01:30.840 --> 00:01:35.750
Oftentimes with these situations, you want
to take the path of least resistance.

00:01:35.750 --> 00:01:40.359
And the path of least resistance initially
might be saying, hey, don't go after her and

00:01:40.359 --> 00:01:42.509
say, never watch Fox News again.

00:01:42.509 --> 00:01:46.590
But it might be add this or that to your media
diet.

00:01:46.590 --> 00:01:49.520
Check out the PBS NewsHour or maybe watch.

00:01:49.520 --> 00:01:50.520
You know what?

00:01:50.520 --> 00:01:53.090
Get more variety in your media diet.

00:01:53.090 --> 00:01:57.990
Maybe read something would be an interesting
one as well, though not everybody reads.

00:01:57.990 --> 00:02:00.140
Consider that the first step.

00:02:00.140 --> 00:02:05.200
And you know, think about it like someone
who's addicted to I don't imagine someone

00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:10.470
every morning has one of those sugary toaster
strudel.

00:02:10.470 --> 00:02:11.730
I don't even know if those are around.

00:02:11.730 --> 00:02:15.720
But I remember when I was a kid that was like
the epitome or like a pop tart or something.

00:02:15.720 --> 00:02:16.720
Okay.

00:02:16.720 --> 00:02:19.050
And please, if you work for those companies,
don't sue me.

00:02:19.050 --> 00:02:20.980
I'm just saying they have a lot of sugar.

00:02:20.980 --> 00:02:26.400
Imagine someone every single day has a toaster
strudel with extra powdered sugar and maple

00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:27.500
sirup and all this stuff.

00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:29.780
And it's like, okay, that's really bad.

00:02:29.780 --> 00:02:34.920
But if we just go in and we say, Just stop,
just stop cold turkey, no more toaster studios.

00:02:34.920 --> 00:02:37.821
You can understand how it would be very difficult
to get that person to say, okay, sure, no

00:02:37.821 --> 00:02:38.940
more Toaster Studios.

00:02:38.940 --> 00:02:40.630
What do they replace it with?

00:02:40.630 --> 00:02:45.840
So if that was what I was dealing with, I
might first go in and go, Hey, you know what?

00:02:45.840 --> 00:02:51.340
It might be interesting just for diversity,
you know, to try different things.

00:02:51.340 --> 00:02:58.130
If one morning a week instead of the toaster
strudel, you instead get a piece of beautiful

00:02:58.130 --> 00:03:04.560
multigrain toast and then spread some avocado
on it with some spicy chili oil.

00:03:04.560 --> 00:03:05.560
Oh, okay.

00:03:05.560 --> 00:03:07.380
Well, now we've got an alternative.

00:03:07.380 --> 00:03:10.040
You're not saying drop the toaster strudel.

00:03:10.040 --> 00:03:14.570
You're saying have six toaster strudel a week
and have one piece of avocado toast.

00:03:14.570 --> 00:03:16.410
And then if that goes, okay, you go, hey,
you know what?

00:03:16.410 --> 00:03:18.660
There's so many great breakfasts.

00:03:18.660 --> 00:03:26.040
What if one morning you had a bowl of Greek
yogurt with sliced up berries and a no sugar

00:03:26.040 --> 00:03:27.040
granola?

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:28.040
It's delicious.

00:03:28.040 --> 00:03:32.570
So now you've got five, two, and then later
you can go, hey, you know, how are you feeling,

00:03:32.570 --> 00:03:33.590
by the way?

00:03:33.590 --> 00:03:38.000
You you feeling any better now that you're
introducing some other and you get the point?

00:03:38.000 --> 00:03:39.000
Okay.

00:03:39.000 --> 00:03:40.470
So this is the same thing I would suggest
with Fox News.

00:03:40.470 --> 00:03:44.560
I would say, hey, you know, there's so many
different media outlets out there.

00:03:44.560 --> 00:03:45.760
Variety is good.

00:03:45.760 --> 00:03:51.100
What if one morning you listen to NPR's Fresh
Air instead of watching Fox and Friends or

00:03:51.100 --> 00:03:55.720
whatever the case may be, start there and
then see where that gets you.

00:03:55.720 --> 00:04:00.670
And you know, it's an uphill battle for sure,
but that's probably what would someone who's

00:04:00.670 --> 00:04:04.530
really addicted, that's probably where I would
start.

